{
  "entity0": {
    "rationale": "Iteration 0 has no race telemetry and no integration feedback, so this is a baseline built from the contract alone. The 25 mm tape needs sensors that can see its edges, and the robot must cover about 4.5 m in under 3 s, so it needs a stable body and wheel layout that can carry roughly 1.5 m/s. I chose five sensors at 12 mm spacing across a 48 mm span. That keeps at least one sensor on the tape across normal tracking error and gives a graded reading near each edge. The sensors sit 40 mm ahead of the axle so the steering reacts before the wheels reach a bend. Track width 0.12 m and body width 0.12 m keep the robot stable in yaw. The off-track limit is then 0.06 m, which gives margin before a run ends. Radius 0.03 m, mass 0.8 kg and body length 0.18 m are mid-range values that keep inertia moderate. Expected result: a first race that completes the oval and s-bend with few line-loss events. The main uncertainty is whether a 12 mm sensor footprint with 12 mm spacing gives a smooth enough signal for the Integrator's gains.",
    "geometry": {
      "sensor_positions": [
        {"x": -0.024, "y": 0.04},
        {"x": -0.012, "y": 0.04},
        {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.04},
        {"x": 0.012, "y": 0.04},
        {"x": 0.024, "y": 0.04}
      ],
      "sensor_size": 0.012,
      "wheel_track": 0.12,
      "wheel_radius": 0.03,
      "body_width": 0.12,
      "body_length": 0.18,
      "mass": 0.8
    },
    "intent": "Baseline symmetric five-sensor array with 12 mm spacing and 12 mm footprints, 40 mm ahead of the axle, to give the Integrator a clean, balanced platform. The sensor weights are linear (-2,-1,0,1,2) so the signal scales with lateral offset. I expect a first race that completes with low line-loss events, and I will use the measured error to decide whether to narrow or widen the array and move it forward or back.",
    "feedback_request": {
      "questions": [
        "Is the five-sensor 12 mm spacing too coarse or too fine for stable steering at the gains you chose?",
        "Did the robot lose the line at any point, and on which track feature?",
        "Would more forward sensor offset (y) or a wider array (x span) have helped the controller?",
        "Is the 0.8 kg mass and 0.12 m track width giving enough turn authority at base_speed near 1.5?"
      ]
    },
    "learning": "No race evidence yet. Hypotheses to test: (1) a 12 mm footprint with 12 mm spacing gives enough overlap for a smooth signal; (2) sensors 40 mm ahead of the axle give enough lead to avoid late corrections on tight bends; (3) mass near 0.8 kg with a 0.12 m track keeps the robot responsive without slip at 1.5 m/s.",
    "_presentation_note": "Baseline geometry from contract alone; no race data yet."
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor array",
      "notes": "Symmetric five-sensor array at 12 mm spacing, 12 mm footprints, 40 mm ahead of the axle, on a mid-range 0.8 kg body. No race evidence exists yet, so this is a contract-based starting point to test sensing coverage and turn authority."
